<%# The same `remaining` value as inside the island below — reactive
    values match document-wide, so a placeholder OUTSIDE the island (a
    header badge) updates too, and every site keeps its own tag/styling
    (a <strong> here, a <span> below). %>
<h1>Hibiki cable spike — todos (Phlex) — <%= reactive :remaining, 0, tag_name: :strong %> left</h1>

<%# This page runs on the packaged client (hibiki_rails's vendored
    Stimulus controller + Helpers): one channel subscription both ways,
    no Turbo stream and no stream_connected wait — `received` is
    registered at subscribe time, so the render effect's first transmit
    always lands. The counter page deliberately stays on the
    Turbo-broadcast transport as its live proof.

    `island` is the ERB block spelling of the root (0.12.0): it folds the
    hibiki_island splat and, by default, the channel's turbo_stream_from;
    `transport: :transmit` is this transport — no stream source inside. %>
<%= island TodosChannel, cid: @cid, transport: :transmit do %>
  <%# A throwaway instance to fill the space on first paint; the channel's
      long-lived instance takes over from its first transmit. %>
  <%= render TodoList.new %>

  <%= tag.form(**on(:add, event: :submit)) do %>
    <input type="text" name="title" placeholder="new todo">
    <button>add</button>
  <% end %>

  <%# The reactive-value shape, live-proven next to the whole-component
      swap above: named placeholders, kept fresh by the channel's
      transmit_value(:remaining) — no fragment class, no extra island.
      The header badge above is the same value's second site. %>
  <p>remaining (reactive value): <%= reactive :remaining, 0 %></p>
<% end %>

<p><a href="/">&larr; ERB stage</a> &middot; <a href="/phlex-counter">Phlex counter &rarr;</a></p>
